
== §1 — SPEC INTEGRITY AND NO DRIFT ==
  ✓ the browser spec is byte-identical to acs_authoring.json
  ✓ schema and engine version are pinned
  ✓ the transaction states are the six declared states
  ✓ the four declared failure states exist
  ✓ DRAFT can never transition straight to COMMITTED
  ✓ no state transitions directly into a mutated model without COMMITTED
  ✓ every declared issue code carries a declared severity
  ✓ every command type declares its owning discipline
  ✓ every implemented command type is part of the declared vocabulary
  ✓ the declared-but-unimplemented set is disjoint from the implemented set
  ✓ every command type is either implemented or explicitly declared unimplemented
  ✓ every implemented command type appears in the dependency graph
  ✓ the whole Part 3 vocabulary is present
  ✓ no arbitrary path-based write type is offered

== §9 — VALIDATION IS NOT CODE COMPLIANCE ==
  ✓ the specification states plainly that validity is not compliance
  ✓ no issue code is named as a code violation
  ✓ the specification declares compliance NOT_EVALUATED
  ✓ the specification carries no building-code vocabulary anywhere
  ✓ the code vocabulary probe is not vacuous

== §2 — COMMAND SCHEMA AND NORMALISATION ==
  ✓ a well-formed command normalises
  ✓ the normalised command carries command_id
  ✓ the normalised command carries command_hash
  ✓ the normalised command carries type
  ✓ the normalised command carries discipline
  ✓ the normalised command carries target_id
  ✓ the normalised command carries parameters
  ✓ the normalised command carries constraints
  ✓ the normalised command carries source
  ✓ the normalised command carries actor_id
  ✓ the normalised command carries base_revision
  ✓ the normalised command carries created_at
  ✓ the normalised command carries status
  ✓ the normalised command carries writes_to_model
  ✓ the command id follows the declared pattern
  ✓ the command declares that it writes nothing by itself
  ✓ the default source is USER
  ✓ an unauthenticated actor is null, never invented
  ✓ the discipline is taken from the specification, not guessed

== §45/§46 — DETERMINISTIC COMMAND IDENTITY ==
  ✓ key order does not change the command hash
  ✓ the same semantic edit hashes the same across repeated calls
  ✓ a timestamp does not affect the semantic command hash
  ✓ an actor does not affect the semantic command hash
  ✓ the source does not affect the semantic command hash
  ✓ a different parameter changes the hash
  ✓ a different target changes the hash
  ✓ a different base revision changes the hash
  ✓ a constraint changes the hash
  ✓ constraint order does not change the hash
  ✓ the hash carries no timestamp or random component

== §41/§47 — UNTRUSTED INPUT IS REFUSED ==
  ✓ normalisation refuses a null command
  ✓ the refusal of a null command uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses a string command
  ✓ the refusal of a string command uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses an array command
  ✓ the refusal of an array command uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses a numeric command
  ✓ the refusal of a numeric command uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses an empty object
  ✓ the refusal of an empty object uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses an unknown type
  ✓ the refusal of an unknown type uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses an array used as a type
  ✓ the refusal of an array used as a type uses a declared code
  ✓ normalisation refuses a numeric type
  ✓ the refusal of a numeric type uses a declared code
  ✓ a path-based write type (forbidden_set_field) is refused as not allowed
  ✓ a path-based write type (forbidden_patch) is refused as not allowed
  ✓ a prototype-pollution key (proto_pollution) is refused before processing
  ✓ a prototype-pollution key (constructor_key) is refused before processing
  ✓ a prototype-pollution attempt does not pollute Object.prototype
  ✓ an executable payload (script_value) is refused
  ✓ an executable payload (javascript_url) is refused
  ✓ an executable payload (eval_value) is refused
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (nan_delta) is judged without throwing
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (nan_delta) never reaches a model as a number
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (inf_delta) is judged without throwing
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (inf_delta) never reaches a model as a number
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (bool_delta) is judged without throwing
  ✓ a non-numeric delta (bool_delta) never reaches a model as a number
  ✓ deep nesting is refused
  ✓ an over-long string is refused
  ✓ the authoring engine uses no eval, no exec and no Function constructor

== §41 — DECLARED SNAPPING ONLY ==
  ✓ an unknown snap type is refused and falls back to NONE
  ✓ a declared but unimplemented snap type says so rather than pretending
  ✓ grid snap rounds the parameter to the declared grid
  ✓ snapping happens before hashing, so a snapped edit is one normal form
  ✓ the edit grid is documented as not a structural grid

== §38 — EDITABILITY CONTRACT ==
  ✓ a space exposes an editable property model
  ✓ wall geometry is editable through the space rectangle
  ✓ a computed area is DERIVED, not editable
  ✓ the model hash is DERIVED
  ✓ a render material is DISPLAY_ONLY
  ✓ the source id is READ_ONLY
  ✓ every field carries one of the five declared classes
  ✓ not every displayed property is editable
  ✓ an editable field publishes its validation constraints
  ✓ an opening width is editable
  ✓ a derived host wall reference is DERIVED
  ✓ an unstated clear width is UNKNOWN, never invented
  ✓ a compiled wall exposes no editable geometry of its own
  ✓ a derived element is documented as edited through its source

== §16/§17 — DEPENDENCY GRAPH IS SELECTIVE, NOT BLIND ==
  ✓ a wall move reports its dependency impact
  ✓ a wall move invalidates ARCHITECTURE
  ✓ a wall move invalidates RELATIONSHIPS
  ✓ a wall move invalidates COORDINATION
  ✓ a wall move invalidates VISUAL
  ✓ a wall move invalidates RUNTIME
  ✓ a wall move does not invalidate the structural discipline
  ✓ a wall move does not invalidate MEP
  ✓ a wall move does not invalidate fire and life safety
  ✓ the report states no structural, MEP or FLS element was mutated
  ✓ a window move does not invalidate navigation blindly
  ✓ a rename does not invalidate the whole world
  ✓ a lock invalidates nothing at all
  ✓ deleting a door reports fire and life safety as possibly affected
  ✓ the dependency note explains why STRUCTURE is absent architecturally
  ✓ the impact report is factual and disclaims recommendation

== §18 — CASCADE PREVIEW NAMES EXACT IDS ==
  ✓ a destructive impact names exact element ids, never "some dependencies"
  ✓ the affected count matches the named ids
  ✓ the named ids resolve in the model

== §95 — NO USER OR ROLE IS FABRICATED ==
  ✓ the declared sources are exactly the four allowed
  ✓ a commit without an identity records a null actor
  ✓ no user, role or permission is fabricated — the absence is stated, not implied
  ✓ no permission or role field exists anywhere in the command schema
  ✓ an unknown source is refused rather than accepted as a new identity

== §96 — NO COLLABORATION IS IMPLEMENTED ==
  ✓ no multiplayer, websocket or CRDT vocabulary exists in the specification
  ✓ the revision guard exists as the concurrency foundation instead

